  "result": "Here's the draft. I haven't added it to `README.md`.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nCarrier rate cards live in `shop/carriers/`, one module per carrier (Acme through Tundra, 20 in all). Each module defines a `BASE_RATE` in cents. A quote is that base rate plus a per-unit weight charge, multiplied by a zone factor. Every carrier takes weight in kilograms except **Maple** (`shop/carriers/maple.py`), which takes weight in grams. Convert the weight before you ask Maple for a quote.\n```\n\nIt's about 65 words. I checked it against the code: all 20 carrier modules define `BASE_RATE`. Maple is the only one that works in grams: its docstring says \"weight in grams\" and it uses `MAX_GRAMS` and `PER_GRAMS`. Every other carrier uses `MAX_KG` and `PER_KG`.\n\nThe external model's first draft was accurate but thin, so I added the pricing formula and the note about converting weight for Maple.",
